      "text": "literature has found the pH PZC to be 9.7 ( Coelho et al., 2006 ). GAC with basic pH PZC has been shown to exhibit better PFAS removal performance than those with neutral pH PZC values ( Cantoni et al., 2021 ). 2.2. Pilot Study A pilot-scale facility was operated continuously to treat a ground - water supply with historical industrial PFAS contamination. The pilot evaluated a single-column GAC treatment with a reduced empty-bed contact time for an accelerated data collection timeline. A schematic of the pilot is shown in Fig. 1 , while operational details for the pilot are shown in Table 1 . The pilot employed three 3,785-liter reservoirs fed from a contami - nated municipal well to maintain continuous operation. Prior to entering the reservoirs, water was pretreated using BIRM \u00ae iron removal media (Clack Corporation, Windsor, Wisconsin, United States) from GAC bed volumes of 0 \u2013 44,734, which was later replaced with Filox-R \u2122 media (Watts, North Andover, Massachusetts, United States) to provide iron and manganese removal from GAC bed volumes of 44,734 \u2013 84,249. Following the reservoirs, the water passed through a 1-micron cartridge filter for further pretreatment. The GAC column was fed using a Seepex BW1 metering pump."
